The session plan is written: two task files and the issue responses are in session_plan/. The commit step was a no-op because session_plan/ is gitignored. The plan template expects that (it ends in || true), and the files sit where the implementation phase reads them.

Task 1 (product, "Part of #1138"): stop yoyo panicking when the CA certificate setting points at a bad file. The assessment showed that if SSL_CERT_FILE points at an empty, non-certificate or missing file, yoyo -p crashes with a worker panic and a misleading "reply cut off" note. The task adds a startup check that refuses with a plain message naming the variable, the path, and the fix (point it at a valid certificate bundle, or unset it). Constraints on the implementer:
• Before writing the check, probe each file shape on the built binary, including ones the assessment didn't try. The check refuses only shapes that were shown to panic, and a valid bundle must keep working.
• It runs after shell commands are handled, so yoyo doctor and yoyo grep aren't affected.
• A real-binary test confirms the message appears and "panicked" doesn't, plus one deliberate break of the check to prove the test can fail.

Task 2 (product, "Fixes #1128"): this is the backlog-drain slot. There are 17 open self-filed issues, and #1128 has the least work left (no comments, a narrow done-when). In -p and piped runs, the 💡 error hints suggest REPL commands like /model and /provider that don't exist there. The task searches every hint diagnose_api_error can return for slash commands rather than trusting the two the issue names. One-shot runs get --model / --provider; the REPL text stays exactly as it is now, checked with exact string comparisons. prompt_retry.rs is at its size cap, so the task decides where the extra lines go and updates its size-gate entry in the same diff if needed.

Changes made on GitHub at planning:
• Filed #1138 (upstream label): seven yoagent providers create their HTTP client in a way that panics when it can't be built. That's the root cause of the crash, and yoagent has to fix it. The issue also records a leftover on our side: after a panic, the turn-end note still says "reply cut off".
• Commented on #1137: widened its scope from "writer commands" to any command that prints a failure but exits 0. The new example is skill search exiting 0 when gh fails.

